    {
      "id": "kinetempo-heel-drop-bent",
      "name": "Heel drop — knee bent",
      "description": "The same position, but the working knee stays slightly bent throughout the drop. Bending the knee takes the calf muscle out of the line of pull and moves the load onto the soleus and the tendon itself, which is why the protocol asks for both versions. Rise on both legs, lower on the painful one over three seconds, come back up on both.",
